A||N||23||Archie||IRM, I would like to know||||5||
Z||000000||Archie||09-13-2000||03:58 PM||||I know there have been a couple of threads on IRM lately. Some concern as to wether they are still in business etc.<P>Did you know that IRM is one of the oldest Fiero related businesses, even older than V-8 Archie?<P>I would be Curious to know the Lists' opinions on the IRM product line, thus the following questions....<P>1) Of the many products that IRM has offered, which do you think still have enough appeal to make them worth continuing?<P>2) How many of the products that were originally made by IRM are now being copied by other concerns?<P>3) Several of IRM's body kits that are in their catalog are items that sell in very small quantities these days. Do you think that some of the low volume items would sell if they were widely publicized on the Internet?<P>4) Other than the IMSA body kit and the Intergrated rocker panels, what other IRM products interest you?<P>Thanks<P>Archie||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||09-13-2000||06:54 PM||||Sounds like somebody is contemplating buying out IRM- I think that very few people are aware of the full extant of IRMs products, not being on the internet with nitche products is certianly not an asset. I used to be in the advertising bussiness and word of mouth in this day and age just doesn't cut it. I would think that a market exists for all their products with proper presentation.(Hint buy them and give me stuff and I'll show it all over the place)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> FWIW||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||09-13-2000||07:10 PM||||I have to agree with Phil, I really have no idea what IRM has in their product line. But yes the integrated rockers are awesome.<P>Archie, I think there is much potential in IRM,especially if they marketed properly. With the amount of Fiero owners/worshippers out there, Yes the product line seems worth continuing.<P>Jeff<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-13-2000||08:45 PM||||Last time I spoke with Barbara she wasn't planning on selling, but I guess things can change.  I've never had the opportunity to purchase anything from IRM, but I plan to in the future.  I especially like the Integrated Rocker Panels.  (Archie--If you <I>do</I> buy out IRM, maybe you could make us fellow forum members a good deal on stuff?)  I think all IRM needs to grow is some decent advertising.  A real website, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||09-13-2000||09:08 PM||||A great product I was looking at for myself from their catalog is the flexible stainless steel egr tube. It's got a braided stainless steel cover which makes it resistant to vibration. If they do go out I hope someone will continue to make these. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||2
Z||000005||MikeSchaefer||09-13-2000||09:23 PM||||IRM's stuff is great, but the prices are just too high on almost every product they offer. <BR>Having Fiero merchandise for sale and not using the internet is almost pointless nowadays too, since the community is starting to rely on it so much.<BR>My 2 Cents,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||2
Z||000006||sluppy123||09-13-2000||10:03 PM||||I love their air dam for the non-areo nose coupes. It is built very Very Solid(it's taken quite a few hits, curbs, speed bumps, small rodents...) and really sets off the whole car. I bought it from them about 4 years ago with no problems other than it taking 4-5 weeks for delivery.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian S.<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT||||reg||10
Z||000007||Songman||09-13-2000||10:24 PM||||I looked over the website where someone had scanned their catalog pages and I think they could really have a great business if someone took hold of it and got the word out! There are a lot of products in there that I would be interested in.<P>As I said earlier, I made the offer to do a website for them. Archie, but it and let me get involved through you! heheh||||reg||3
Z||000008||Uaana||09-13-2000||10:35 PM||||Along with those who want in on the mgt side, I avail for setting up the customer service end of the operation, after working with a couple of very large mktg companies one is completly web specific. <BR>And this is to those companies that do business on the web (no offense intended!) But a turn around time of more than 24 hours to an email request or more than a 3 hr reply to a phone request is unacceptable. I know it is hard for the little guys to have a dedicated customer service dept but has any of them/you looked into contracting with a cust serv co?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Patrick's Dad||09-13-2000||10:36 PM||||I have a catalog from about five years back. I liked the Women's Fiero Panties (for my wife....). I always thought (as a photographer, of course) that the girl in the picture should be wearing them, not holding them with her hands.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I have noticed that most of the clothing items have been removed for the Big Fiero Parts Book (1st Ed).<P>On a more serious note, I ordered a hi-flow cat. con. and straight pipes with the resonator tips from them. Whole package was about $420, with shipping. Everything fit where it was supposed to, and it sounds very sweet with no muffler, but now, about four years later, the Hooker tips that came included have rotted (I thought it was the welds, until I looked more closely), and now I am down to one (from four). The stainless, while not metallic in color, is still very much intact.<P>The oil cooler and the steel brake lines were on my list, and the wraparound decklid spoiler, too, as I've had two wings stolen from my car. Actually, now that my car is in the garage, I now have an OEM and an aftermarket spoiler in the garage, too....<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....    <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Patrick's Dad (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000010||2xsess||09-13-2000||11:35 PM||||I've also found that site with the scanned pages of their catalog. Their prices seem quite high. Ah well just my thoughts.<P>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000011||007DOUG||09-13-2000||11:55 PM||||I've bought a ton of IRM stuff. Several of my fieors are "rolling IRM billboards"<P>Out of all the parts I have, these have been the most asked about accessories (in order of popularity):<P>Twin "Over the roof" scoops<BR>Indy scoop<BR>IMSA wing<BR>Intergrated rockers<BR>Rocker panels <BR>Twin dual exhaust<P>There is a big market for the twin & Indy scoops, and the IMSA wing.<P>Stuff like the KONIs, drop spindles, and turbo kits can be bought elsewhere.  I think IRM just "carried" those items.<P>They really need a website.<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||14
Z||000012||cifc||09-14-2000||12:25 AM||||I have to agree with gokart.  The egr tube is great.I went through about 4 of those things from Pontiac. The last one lasted less than a week.  I got IRM's a couple years ago, and no problems since.  That's definitely one of the best Fiero products anyone has brought to market.  I think since then FOCOA is selling one too.  I don't know if it's the same or not.<BR>--Jason ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Philphine||09-14-2000||01:52 AM||||got the integrated rocker panels and indy scoop on my '87 coupe. i'll probaly get a chin spoiler for the gt facia i got for it.  want another scoop for my indy. i'd like to get a good look at the kamie (not sure if i spelled that right) body kit for non gt style coupes if it's still made. itdose take a while to get orders but where else you gonna get 'em.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Oreif||09-14-2000||01:58 AM||||I have bought a few item's from IRM over the years. I think if they had a website they would be piled high with orders. I think the prices are slightly high and have noticed the add on panels, wings, scoops, and such are usually made to order. I think with a little more "on the shelf" items and a website it would be a huge asset. With the larger volume of orders the prices could then be lowered to still keep a healthy profit and be fair to the customers. My Indy scoop took 6 weeks to get. I know others who have bought air dams and had to wait almost 12 weeks to get them.<BR>Archie, If your thinking about buying into them or buying them would you still retain the I-4 and V-6 parts?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||2
